        <link href="https://example.com/blog/first-post/" type="text/html"/>
        <id>https://example.com/blog/first-post/</id>
        <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;This is the &lt;em&gt;first&lt;/em&gt; post. It has a summary, which ends here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;span id=&quot;continue-reading&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;why&quot;&gt;Why&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A generator turns a tree of markdown into a tree of HTML. That is the whole
job, and it is a good one for finding out what a language is like.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;aside class=&quot;note note-tip&quot;&gt;Shortcodes render through templates.&lt;/aside&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;how&quot;&gt;How&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-rust&quot; data-lang=&quot;rust&quot;&gt;fn main() {
    println!(&amp;quot;&amp;lt;hello&amp;gt;&amp;quot;);
}
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;a-smaller-heading&quot;&gt;A smaller heading&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read the &lt;a href=&quot;https://example.com/blog/second-post/#tables&quot;&gt;second post&lt;/a&gt; next.&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
